 This install applies to "Revs", an unofficial Amiga port of the 1985 BBC
 Micro Formula 3 racing simulation by Geoff Crammond, published by Acornsoft.
 It is the "Revs Plus Revs 4 Tracks" release: Silverstone, Brands Hatch,
 Donington Park, Oulton Park and Snetterton, plus the Nurburgring.

 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad version 17.0 or better and a PAL Amiga with at
 least 2 MB of RAM. The installed program uses 400 KB ChipMem and 768 KB
 OtherMem.

 The game also requires an A500 Kickstart 1.3 image named "kick34005.A500" in
 "Devs:Kickstarts". It can be extracted from an A500 with GrabKick or a similar
 tool. The matching relocation file "kick34005.A500.RTB", found in the Aminet
 archive "util/boot/skick346.lha", must be placed in the same directory.

 Without WHDLoad the game runs from Workbench or a Shell on any PAL Amiga with
 Kickstart 1.3 or better, a 68000 or better, 512 KB ChipMem and 512 KB of other
 memory. It then needs the disc image (see below) as "revs.ssd" next to it.
 Shell users on Kickstart 1.3 must change to the game's drawer first.


 Installation:
 -------------
 The install does not include the original game. Before running it, download
 either of these BBC Micro disc images from bbcmicro.co.uk:

 Revs Plus Revs 4 Tracks:  https://www.bbcmicro.co.uk/game.php?id=2203
                           DiscA15-RevsPlusRevs4Tracks.ssd, SHA-256
   d014b19d58e5bb1616b8a5ab089c8f27d31d1b37f9bd7d78b936367cf4725afd
 Revs+ [hack]:             https://www.bbcmicro.co.uk/game.php?id=4179
                           DiscA16-RevsHack.ssd, SHA-256
   571f6dede00c702917e94cda2cca28245ef4fb30e41df81c806a8729de9e0792

 If the download is a ZIP archive, extract the .ssd file from it first. Run the
 Install icon and, when asked for the disc image, select the .ssd file. Its
 filename does not matter: the installer copies it to the game drawer as
 "revs.ssd". Both images are 204800 bytes and carry the same game engine; the
 circuits are built into the port, so either one gives all six.

 The game checks the disc image when it starts and reads the engine from it.
 If the check fails, make sure the file is one of the two images above and not
 another version of Revs (the 1985 single-circuit and "Revs 4 Tracks" discs
 carry an older engine and are not supported).


 Controls:
 ---------
 The keys are the BBC Micro's: L and ; steer (or the cursor keys), S is the
 throttle and A the brake (or up and down), Q and Tab change gear, T is the
 starter and Space fine steering. SHIFT+F2 selects mouse steering, where the
 right mouse button accelerates, the left one brakes and the middle one changes
 gear. The other SHIFT+function key commands are as in the original manual,
 with the BBC's f0 on F10 and COPY (pause) on Help.


 Quitting:
 ---------
 The game can be quit by pressing CTRL-Q, immediately and without
 confirmation, at any point in the game. The WHDLoad QuitKey (keypad "*", key
 can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=") works only on a 68010 or better. F10
 is not the QuitKey, because it is a game key.


